        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The marginal is therefore $p_i=q_i e^{r_i}/C$, where $C:=\\sum_jq_je^{r_j}$. The bounds $e^{-\\delta}\\le e^{r_j}\\le e^\\delta$ and $\\sum_jq_j=1$ imply $e^{-\\delta}\\le C\\le e^\\delta$, so $e^{-2\\delta}\\le p_i/q_i\\le e^{2\\delta}$.",
          "step": "2.1",
