            "source_excerpt": "For every fixed $\\beta>0$, the sequence $p_L(\\beta)$ of [[def-tdmath-bounded-finite-range-lattice]] has a finite limit as $L\\to\\infty$. If another finite-volume energy $\\widetilde H_L$ on the same configurations satisfies $\\sup_s|\\widetilde H_L(s)-H_L(s)|\\le C_bL^{d-1}$ for a constant $C_b$ independent of $L$, define $\\widetilde Z_L(\\beta):=\\sum_{s\\in\\mathcal A^{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta\\widetilde H_L(s)}$ and $\\widetilde p_L(\\beta):=L^{-d}\\log\\widetilde Z_L(\\beta)$. Then $\\widetilde p_L$ has the same limit. The result covers finite-alphabet, bounded, translation-invariant finite-range interactions on cubic boxes; it asserts no continuum-particle or long-range limit.",
