          "reason": "Let a finite canonical model have energies $E_i$, ground energy $E_0$, and exactly $g\\ge1$ states at $E_0$, with every other energy strictly larger. Boundary empty: The claim has no empty-set or empty-domain assertion; its stated object domain is nonempty or the boundary is not separate.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let a finite canonical model have energies $E_i$, ground energy $E_0$, and exactly $g\\ge1$ states at $E_0$, with every other energy strictly larger. As $\\beta\\to+\\infty$, each ground-state probability tends to $1/g$, each excited-state probability tends to zero, and the Shannon entropy $-\\sum_i p_i(\\beta)\\log p_i(\\beta)$ tends to $\\log g$. This is a finite-model statement only.",
