          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Definition",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $I$ be a finite or countably infinite set with a specified enumeration, let $E_i\\in\\mathbb R$, and let $\\ell^2(I):=\\{x:I\\to\\mathbb C:\\sum_i|x_i|^2<\\infty\\}$ with inner product $\\langle x,y\\rangle=\\sum_i x_i\\overline{y_i}$, linear in the first variable. Write $u_i$ for the coordinate unit vector at $i$. The diagonal multiplication operator $H_E$ is the linear operator with domain $D(H_E):=\\{x\\in\\ell^2(I):\\sum_i|E_ix_i|^2<\\infty\\}$ and action $(H_Ex)_i:=E_ix_i$. [[lem-tdmath-diagonal-model-hilbert-and-domain]] proves completeness of the coefficient space, linearity and density of this domain, and linearity of the coordinate action before the Hilbert-space operator interpretation is used. Its domain is part of the operator data in the sense of [[def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph]].",
            "current_raw_sha256": "5995970439fcf3751393be5242d38cd1c2893b162565a04c1dd6e2493642c851",
